GAL16V8
BE6502DEC

A15  A14  A13  A12  A11  A10  NC   NC   NC   GND
NC   SIDCS ROMCE ACIACS LCDCS NC  NC   NC   NC   VCC

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; Ben Eater 6502 address decoder - replaces both 74HC138s and the 74HC00.
; Purely combinatorial. Assemble with galasm:  galasm BE6502DEC.pld
;
; $4800-$4BFF  SID / SIDKick pico   (kept, so existing software works)
; $4C00-$4FFF  LCD latch            (spare - wire it when you want it)
; $5000-$53FF  W65C51 ACIA
; $D400-$D7FF  SID again, native C64 address, so .sid files run unpatched
; ROM enabled for $8000-$FFFF EXCEPT the $D400 kilobyte
;
; Still free: $4000-$47FF and $5400-$5FFF, plus three unused outputs and
; four unused inputs. Add equations and re-burn.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

; $D400 = 1101 0100 ....   A15 A14 /A13 A12 /A11 A10
; $4800 = 0100 1000 ....  /A15 A14 /A13 /A12 A11 /A10
/SIDCS  =  A15 *  A14 * /A13 *  A12 * /A11 *  A10
        + /A15 *  A14 * /A13 * /A12 *  A11 * /A10

; $4C00 = 0100 1100 ....  /A15 A14 /A13 /A12 A11 A10
/LCDCS  = /A15 *  A14 * /A13 * /A12 *  A11 *  A10

; $5000 = 0101 0000 ....  /A15 A14 /A13 A12 /A11 /A10
/ACIACS = /A15 *  A14 * /A13 *  A12 * /A11 * /A10

; ROM on for A15=1, off across $D400-$D7FF. De Morgan on the exclusion:
; NOT(A14 * /A13 * A12 * /A11 * A10) = /A14 + A13 + /A12 + A11 + /A10
/ROMCE  =  A15 * /A14
        +  A15 *  A13
        +  A15 * /A12
        +  A15 *  A11
        +  A15 * /A10

DESCRIPTION

Five product terms is the widest equation here; a GAL16V8 gives eight per
output, so there is room to add selects as the machine grows. Six of the ten
available inputs are used.

Pin 1 and pin 11 are inputs, which puts the part in simple mode. Note pins 15
and 16 have no feedback path in that mode - not needed here, but it matters if
outputs are ever fed back.
